          "text": "filename: docs/PIPELINE.md\n```markdown\n## Building\n\nThe build process compiles the source code into executable binaries using a standard build toolchain.  \n```bash\nmake build\n```\nThis command runs the `build` target in the Makefile, compiling all C and C++ source files into object files and linking them into the final executable.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe testing phase runs unit and integration tests to ensure code correctness and stability.  \n```bash\nmake test\n```\nThis command executes all test cases defined in the `test/` directory using the built-in test runner, reporting failures and coverage statistics.\n\n## Packaging\n\nThe packaging step creates a distributable archive of the application for deployment.  \n```bash\nmake package\n```\nThis command generates a compressed tarball with the binary, configuration files, and documentation, ready for distribution to production environments.\n\n## Summary\nThe pipeline ensures that code is built, tested, and packaged consistently and reliably. Each stage is automated and verified to maintain code quality and reduce human error.\n```",
